From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:43:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] core: resolve paths, env vars and platform for Android

BepInEx assumes a desktop filesystem layout: config and plugins live next to
the executable, and EnvVars is a thin wrapper over PATH-like lookups. On
Android the launcher unpacks the framework into app-specific external storage
and hands the location over through NEXT_* environment variables, so Paths,
Utility and EnvVars have to follow that contract instead.

PlatformUtils gains an Android branch so PlatformDetection reports
OSKind.Android, which is what selects the IL2CPP runtime, the Android console
driver and the native detour provider.
